  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Evaluating the Lively Minds Early Childhood Care and Education Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A large scale randomized control trial (RCT) is being conducted of a program that supports quality pre-school education in Ghana and Uganda, the intervention seeks to improve childrens health, cognitive and socio-emotional development, and their home and school environments. It trains volunteer women from local villages to run weekly, hour-long play sessions in which children participate in fun, interactive games that strengthen their cognitive, language, and social and emotional skills. It also encourages handwashing and provides monthly parenting courses that teach caregivers simple ways to improve home-based care, including nutrition, hygiene, and malaria prevention.</narrative>
  </description>
